From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/26] egl: surfaceless window surfaces on a CAMetalLayer

The surfaceless platform has pbuffers only, and eglCreateWindowSurface
fails on it by the EGL_MESA_platform_surfaceless spec. Wine's win32u
drives OpenGL through a surfaceless display and needs a window surface
to present to; on iOS that is the CAMetalLayer the app gives a window.

On Apple systems, when the display's driver is Zink with kopper:
- the configs carry EGL_WINDOW_BIT as well as EGL_PBUFFER_BIT
  (dri2_add_pbuffer_configs_for_visuals takes the surface type);
- eglCreateWindowSurface takes a CAMetalLayer as the native window;
- the kopper loader fills VkMetalSurfaceCreateInfoEXT with the layer and
  presents opaque (an alpha below one would show what is behind the
  layer), and takes the surface's size from the layer's drawableSize,
  which the EGL client sets to the size it renders at, or bounds times
  contentsScale before it has one (platform_surfaceless_metal.m);
- swap, swap interval (0 to 1, from dri2_setup_swap_interval) and buffer
  age go to kopper, and a swap updates the surface's size.

Pbuffers, and every other platform and system, are unchanged.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-11-mesa-gl-ios-build.md
Offered-upstream: no
